Dialogue: 2,0:01:29.40,0:01:34.36,Chinese,C01-04-zh-5,0,0,0,,{\q2}它们都会影响我们对“恢复了”“少人了”“停下了”的判断。
Dialogue: 1,0:01:29.78,0:01:30.05,English,C01-04-en-5,0,0,0,,{\q2}leg.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:30.05,0:01:33.93,English,C01-04-en-6,0,0,0,,{\q2}These affect what we mean by 'recovered,' 'lost troops' and
Dialogue: 1,0:01:33.93,0:01:38.33,English,C01-04-en-7,0,0,0,,{\q2}'stopped.' We will examine the actual records before explaining the
Dialogue: 2,0:01:34.36,0:01:38.79,Chinese,C01-04-zh-6,0,0,0,,{\q2}接下来分别看实际记录，再解释这些变化。
Dialogue: 1,0:01:38.33,0:01:38.86,English,C01-04-en-8,0,0,0,,{\q2}changes.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:39.53,0:01:42.67,English,C01-05-en-0,0,0,0,,{\q2}Troops can be lost through different processes.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:39.53,0:01:42.38,Chinese,C01-05-zh-0,0,0,0,,{\q2}兵员减少也有不同入口。
Dialogue: 2,0:01:42.38,0:01:47.48,Chinese,C01-05-zh-1,0,0,0,,{\q2}围城和劫掠的周期处理、进入新县时的移动损耗，各
Dialogue: 1,0:01:42.67,0:01:46.81,English,C01-05-en-1,0,0,0,,{\q2}Periodic siege and raid processing, and movement attrition on
Dialogue: 1,0:01:46.81,0:01:51.15,English,C01-05-en-2,0,0,0,,{\q2}entering a new county, have their own conditions and calculation
Dialogue: 2,0:01:47.48,0:01:52.35,Chinese,C01-05-zh-2,0,0,0,,{\q2}自有条件和计算顺序；不能把每次少人都叫饥饿。
Dialogue: 1,0:01:51.15,0:01:51.56,English,C01-05-en-3,0,0,0,,{\q2}order.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:51.56,0:01:53.50,English,C01-05-en-4,0,0,0,,{\q2}Not every loss is starvation.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:52.35,0:01:55.54,Chinese,C01-05-zh-3,0,0,0,,{\q2}与此同时，补员、分合军或其
Dialogue: 1,0:01:53.50,0:01:58.64,English,C01-05-en-5,0,0,0,,{\q2}Replenishment, splitting, merging and other events can also change the total.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:55.54,0:01:58.72,Chinese,C01-05-zh-4,0,0,0,,{\q2}他事件也会改变看到的总数。
Dialogue: 1,0:01:58.64,0:02:02.35,English,C01-05-en-6,0,0,0,,{\q2}To explain a march, first compare each regiment's exact
Dialogue: 2,0:01:58.72,0:02:02.84,Chinese,C01-05-zh-5,0,0,0,,{\q2}要解释一段行军，先逐团核对前后整数，
